    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Utilizing field observations and paleocurrent directions, several Miocene age sedimentary basins are analyzed, and their relations to major faults, including the Las Vegas shear zone and the Bitter Spring Valley fault in southeastern Nevada, are examined. The analysis provides additional support for previous conclusion that a mid-Miocene and a late-Miocene basin are direct consequences of a two-stage structural history of the Las Vegas shear zone.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
